<title>USA: Alternative Living buys residences.</title>
<headline>Alternative Living buys residences.</headline>
<dateline>BROOKFIELD, Wis. 1997-06-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>Alternative Living Services Inc, which operates assisted living residences, entered into an agreement to purchase two neighboring free-standing residences for the elderly in Reno, Nev., with a combined capacity of 155 units.</p>
<p>The acquisition represents an investment by the company of approximately $13.3 million.</p>
<p>The transaction is anticipated to close on or before June 30.</p>
<p>Alternative Living currently operates 88 residences in 14 states.</p>
<p>((Reuters Chicago Newsdesk (312) 408-8787))</p>
